<%- include('partials/head') %>
<div class="landing">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="landing-top">
      <a class="brand-lockup" href="/"><img src="/img/logo.svg" alt="" class="brand-logo" width="32" height="32"><span class="brand-name">HisabFlow</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/auth/login">Sign in</a>
    </div>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="row g-4 g-lg-5 align-items-center">
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <h1>Write the khata the way you’d say it.</h1>
          <p class="lead">Type <span class="sample">“Meena took 2 kg sugar at 45 and a litre of oil for 130, paid 100.”</span> HisabFlow splits it into items, rates and a payment. You check the preview, then it goes into her ledger.</p>
          <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/auth/register" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Start your khata</a>
            <a href="/auth/login" class="btn btn-quiet btn-lg">Sign in</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <div class="paper" role="img" aria-label="Example of a typed sentence turned into an itemised entry">
            <p class="paper-label">You type</p>
            <div class="typed sample">Meena took 2 kg sugar at 45 and 1 litre oil 130, paid 100</div>
            <p class="paper-label mt-3">HisabFlow reads</p>
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th class="num">Qty</th><th class="num">Rate</th><th class="num">Amount</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Sugar</td><td class="num">2 kg</td><td class="num">₹45</td><td class="num">₹90</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Oil</td><td class="num">1 L</td><td class="num">₹130</td><td class="num">₹130</td></tr>
              </tbody>
              <tfoot>
                <tr><td colspan="3">Credit</td><td class="num"><span class="amt amt-credit">+₹220</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td colspan="3">Paid now</td><td class="num"><span class="amt amt-payment">−₹100</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td colspan="3">Still to collect</td><td class="num">₹120</td></tr>
              </tfoot>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="row g-4 g-lg-5">
        <div class="col-lg-5">
          <h2>Say it however comes naturally.</h2>
          <p>Names, items, quantities, rates and payments can come in any order. You always see what was understood before anything is saved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <ul class="phrases">
            <li><q>Meena took rice 5 kg 300</q><span>Rice, 5 kg, ₹300 credit</span></li>
            <li><q>3 notebooks at 40 each for Ravi</q><span>3 × ₹40 = ₹120 credit</span></li>
            <li><q>received 500 from Anita</q><span>₹500 payment</span></li>
            <li><q>Kumar udhaar 250</q><span>₹250 credit</span></li>
            <li><q>Priya cleared her dues</q><span>Pays off the full balance</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="row g-4 g-lg-5">
        <div class="col-lg-5">
          <h2>A short list for each morning.</h2>
          <p>Customers with money pending are ranked by how much they owe and how long since they last paid. Every name on the list shows the reason it is there.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <table class="rank-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Signal</th><th>Adds to priority</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>No payment for 7 / 14 / 30+ days</td><td>Low / medium / high</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Balance under ₹500</td><td>Low</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Balance ₹500 or more</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Balance ₹1,000 or more</td><td>High</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
